      "notes": "Hint 3 lets the student answer without thinking once it is read after hint 2. Hint 2 already rules out the catalyst by name of concept: 'it changes neither the position of equilibrium nor Kc.' Hint 3 then says, in one sentence, 'Changing concentration or pressure moves the position, but the mixture then adjusts until the ratio Kc is back to its old value.' That single sentence explicitly clears both remaining wrong options (pressure and concentration), so by the closing question, 'Which factor makes the ratio itself settle at a new value?', three of the four options (catalyst, pressure, concentration) have been named and ruled out and only temperature is left unaddressed. The student does not need to reason about temperature at all, only notice it is the one option nothing has excluded yet, which fails the requirement that a student who reads all three hints must still make the choice.",
